{
  "id": "restore-ip-addresses-count",
  "questionId": "restore-ip-addresses-count",
  "slug": "restore-ip-addresses-count",
  "title": "Count of Valid IP Address Restorations",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Backtracking",
  "patterns": [
    "backtracking"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "each of the 4 segments can only be 1, 2, or 3 digits long - that's a very small branching factor per step",
    "recurse with (position in s, segments placed so far); at each call, try taking the next 1, 2, or 3 digits as the next segment",
    "immediately reject a candidate segment if it has a leading zero and more than 1 digit, or if its numeric value exceeds 255 - don't wait until the end to check",
    "count a complete restoration once you've placed exactly 4 segments and consumed the entire string at the same time - both conditions must hold together, not just one"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "allowing a segment like \"012\" or \"00\" that has a leading zero but is more than one digit",
    "not checking that the entire string is consumed exactly when 4 segments have been placed, which can undercount or overcount",
    "allowing a segment value above 255, e.g. treating \"256\" as valid"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a string of digits.\n\n**Count how many ways it can be split into exactly 4 pieces, in order, such that each piece forms a valid IP address segment: a number between 0 and 255, written with no leading zeros (except the single digit \"0\" itself).**\n\nEvery digit in the original string must be used, and the pieces must appear in the same order they occur in the string.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "s consists only of digit characters",
      "4 <= length of s <= 12",
      "each of the 4 segments must be an integer from 0 to 255 with no leading zeros unless the segment is exactly \"0\""
    ],
    "notes": [
      "string length exactly 4 (each character must be its own segment)",
      "string containing zeros that would create invalid leading-zero segments",
      "no valid restoration exists (answer is 0)"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"25525511135\"",
        "output": "2",
        "expectedOutput": "2",
        "explanation": "the two valid restorations are 255.255.11.135 and 255.255.111.35"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"0000\"",
        "output": "1",
        "expectedOutput": "1",
        "explanation": "the only valid restoration is 0.0.0.0"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "s = \"101023\"",
        "output": "5",
        "expectedOutput": "5",
        "explanation": "1.0.10.23, 1.0.102.3, 10.1.0.23, 10.10.2.3, and 101.0.2.3 are all valid"
      }
    ],
